> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based on the detailed README and changelog you provided, here is a structured summary of the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection. This project is a specialized optimization suite for **llama.cpp** targeting **AMD RDNA** GPUs (specifically RDNA3, 3.5, and 4), delivering significant performance gains, memory savings, and new model support.

### 🚀 Core Value Proposition
This is a **16-patch set** (Block 00 + Blocks 01–15) designed to be applied on6.20.555.429 I sched_graph_realloc: graph reallocation: nodes = 5217 (changed = 0), splits = 50, n_same = 7, n_diff = 0
 top of the `llama.cpp` fork point **`790cf516.20.996.762 I slot print_timing: id  0 | task 0 | n_gen =    138, tg =  45.49 t/s, tg_3s =  45.81 t/s
aa`**. It transforms the standard backend into a high-performance engine for AMD hardware, featuring:
*   **Massive VRAM Savings:** Up to ~3.4 GiB saved per GPU on specific models via attention-memory optimizations.
*   **Speed Boosts:** New kernels for Flash Attention, MoE (Mixture of Experts), and quantized decoding.
*   **New Model Support:** Native support for **Qwen4exp** (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) and MTP (Multi-Token Prediction).
*   **Architecture Specificity:** Heavily optimized for **RDNA4 (gfx120x)**, with back-ported optimizations for RDNA3/3.5.6.24.014.267 I slot print_timing: id  0 | task 0 | n_gen =    287, tg =  47.43 t/s, tg_3s =  49.38 t/s


